# The lock file and package.json drift apart silently.
#
# Several dependencies (sharp, Tailwind's oxide binary) declare optional
# packages per platform. Installing on macOS records the native path and omits
# the WebAssembly fallback that Linux needs, so `npm install` leaves a lock
# file that works here and fails on the CI runner with EUSAGE. It has happened
# twice; both times the first sign was a red pipeline.
#
# `npm ci --dry-run` resolves the lock file against package.json without
# installing anything, and takes well under a second. Fix by regenerating from
# scratch, which records every platform's optional dependencies:
#
#   rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json && npm install
npm ci --dry-run
